From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yugidraft <yugidraft@localhost>
Date: Wed, 16 Feb 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: one seat for the disabled zones and the place prompt,
 SSet needs a living toplayer at n > 2

Duel.SelectDisableField offered the zones of the next duelist in turn
order, while the EFFECT_DISABLE_FIELD high half binds to the opponent of the
effect. With the F5 fold, that opponent is the bound one. Scripts that read
the zones back (39 cards use the opponent masks) could disable zones of one
seat after the prompt named another. Duel.SelectFieldZone and the disable
effect could also use different seats (c10584050).

The prompt now names the bound opponent (f8_place_target: scope_bound_opp or
the chain binding, else the next living opponent) for both
Duel.SelectDisableField and Duel.SelectFieldZone, and remembers it in
core.zone_prompt_opp. Duel.RegisterEffect of an EFFECT_DISABLE_FIELD effect
records the bound opponent in the effect (disfield_opp), and an operation
based effect keeps the opponent of the last zone prompt. add_disabled_zones_n
(refresh_location_info_instant and RefreshLoc, both cases) takes that seat
for the high half, else the next living opponent as before. An opponent that
is dead or on the own team is not used.

Duel.SSet to another field checked is_duelist(toplayer) only. At n > 2 it now
checks is_alive(toplayer) too, so a dead seat cannot get a card.

n == 2 is unchanged: the guards keep the old paths, the same bytes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UrYy4jjEcbJHKdcVYasfdb
